From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirk <hello@kirkdiamond.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: turn off the iMac Pro 5K per-frame tile reset

On an iMac Pro the merged panel stalled at login and on resume: a page
flip on the left tile was never completed ("flip_done timed out", then
dm_arm_vblank_event() warns that the previous flip is still pending),
also with amdgpu.imac5k_swap_lock=0.

The per-frame reset of the right tile is the cause. On DCE its only
trigger is GSL group 0, and a GSL group with the surface flip purpose
holds each member's flips until all of them have one; the one-time sync
leaves the group straight away for that reason. A commit that flips the
left tile alone, as happens around login and resume, then never
completes. With the reset off the panel logs in and resumes cleanly.

It is not needed either: after the one-time sync when the tiles are
enabled, both run from the same reference clock with the same timing.
amdgpu_dm_imac5k_genlock read a constant -17 px (35 ns) offset of the
right tile over ten minutes without it, the same as with it, and no
seam tearing was visible.

Add amdgpu.imac5k_genlock, off by default, to keep the per-frame reset
available, and amdgpu.imac5k_tile_lock (default on) to stop holding both
tiles' update locks across a page flip, for comparison.

Written with an AI coding assistant (Claude Code, Claude Opus 5.5) from
iMac Pro hardware tests; tested on an iMac Pro (iMacPro1,1, Fedora 45):
login without flip_done timeouts, genlock offset steady.

Signed-off-by: Kirk <hello@kirkdiamond.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h
@@ -204,6 +204,8 @@
 extern int amdgpu_imac5k_merge;
 extern int amdgpu_imac5k_early_dc;
 extern int amdgpu_imac5k_swap_lock;
+extern int amdgpu_imac5k_genlock;
+extern int amdgpu_imac5k_tile_lock;
 extern uint amdgpu_dc_debug_mask;
 extern uint amdgpu_dc_visual_confirm;
 extern int amdgpu_dm_abm_level;
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
@@ -232,6 +232,8 @@
 int amdgpu_imac5k_merge = 1;
 int amdgpu_imac5k_early_dc = -1;
 int amdgpu_imac5k_swap_lock;
+int amdgpu_imac5k_genlock;
+int amdgpu_imac5k_tile_lock = 1;
 int amdgpu_reset_method = -1; /* auto */
 int amdgpu_num_kcq = -1;
 int amdgpu_smartshift_bias;
@@ -977,6 +979,28 @@
 module_param_named(imac5k_swap_lock, amdgpu_imac5k_swap_lock, int, 0444);
 
 /**
+ * DOC: imac5k_genlock (int)
+ * On the iMac Pro, reset the right panel tile's timing to the left one's on
+ * every frame. Off by default: the tiles do not drift after the one-time
+ * sync when they are enabled, and keeping them in a GSL group for the reset
+ * holds the left tile's flips until the right one flips too, which stalls
+ * the panel at login and on resume. 0 = off (default), 1 = on.
+ */
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(imac5k_genlock,
+		 "Realign the iMac Pro 5K panel tiles every frame (0 = off (default), 1 = on)");
+module_param_named(imac5k_genlock, amdgpu_imac5k_genlock, int, 0444);
+
+/**
+ * DOC: imac5k_tile_lock (int)
+ * On the iMac Pro, hold both panel tiles' update locks while a page flip
+ * programs them, so both halves change on the same frame. 1 = on (default),
+ * 0 = off.
+ */
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(imac5k_tile_lock,
+		 "Latch both iMac Pro 5K panel tiles' flips together (1 = on (default), 0 = off)");
+module_param_named(imac5k_tile_lock, amdgpu_imac5k_tile_lock, int, 0444);
+
+/**
  * DOC: reset_method (int)
  * GPU reset method (-1 = auto (default), 0 = legacy, 1 = mode0, 2 = mode1, 3 = mode2, 4 = baco)
  */
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -4357,7 +4357,7 @@
 	struct drm_crtc *crtc;
 	int i;
 
-	if (!comp)
+	if (!comp || !amdgpu_imac5k_tile_lock)
 		return false;
 
 	comp_state = drm_atomic_get_new_crtc_state(state, comp);
@@ -5828,7 +5828,8 @@
 
 	*count = 0;
 
-	if (context->streams[0]->ctx->dce_version >= DCE_VERSION_MAX)
+	if (!amdgpu_imac5k_genlock ||
+	    context->streams[0]->ctx->dce_version >= DCE_VERSION_MAX)
 		return false;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < context->stream_count; i++) {
-- 
2.47.3

